From: CarPlay C0 lane (2026-11-22)
Subject: 0521 sweet_nub: never release the manually built controller instance

0520 fixed the metaclass accounting and still died at 10.192 s, one line after "manual ->":
  Break 0x0001 instruction exception from kernel. Panic (by design) at pc 0xfffffff004cee5c0
That PC is vtable slot 1 of the published controller vtable, and disassembling the 0520 prelink
shows slots 0 and 1 are literally `brk #1` while slot 2 is getMetaClass -- the two Itanium
destructor slots are traps. OSObject::free() ends with `delete this`, so releasing a manually
built instance dispatches the deleting destructor into that trap. Apple's own instances never
take that path (kext objects are not individually freed), which is why the table can carry the
trap at all.

0521 therefore never releases the manual instance: one 504-byte object leaks per boot, and the
retain() stays (the object must look owned while init/attach/start run). It also prints the
three vtable slots so the next boot proves the layout, and notes the reason in the source.

